Under `--modular-termination` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/211), a library may now record the trusted premises of the built-in standard-library trust list, with the hidden option `--modular-termination-trust:standard-library`.  The list holds the 19 `{:axiom}` lemmas and ghost functions of `Std.Axioms`, `Std.Ordinal` and `Std.Strings`, each bound to digests of its statement and context; any other premise, or a listed one whose statement or context changed, is still refused.  A client admits such a library only when it selects the same list, and its verification summary and `dafny audit` name the premises.  `Source/DafnyStandardLibraries/modular-termination/trusted` builds the standard-library core with `Axioms`, `RealCompleteness` and `Ordinal`.  With the default, `--modular-termination-trust:none`, and without `--modular-termination`, nothing changes.
